' The stage set's per-connection session class -- see tbxStage.twin for why a
' stage set exists, and tbxStageServices.twin for why a Class needs its own file.
'
' WinNamedPipesLib's CustomData slot exists so that a server can hang its own
' per-client object off each connection, and the NamedPipeServerConnection and
' NamedPipeClientConnection pages show that with a class they call
' ClientSession. It is the READER's class, not the package's: no page declares
' it, and none should, because the whole point of CustomData is that the
' package never sees the type.
'
' The members are exactly the ones the pages call, with the signatures their
' call sites imply -- HandleMessage and HandleReply take the events' transient
' Data() As Byte, RemoteId is assigned a connection Handle, and Cleanup takes
' nothing.

[COMCreatable(False)]
Class ClientSession

    Public RemoteId As LongPtr

    Public Sub HandleMessage(ByRef Data() As Byte)
    End Sub

    Public Sub HandleReply(ByRef Data() As Byte)
    End Sub

    Public Sub Cleanup()
    End Sub

End Class
